{"baseRefName":"main","body":"## Result and exact sense\nAn explicit finite algebraic reformulation of Markov equivalence using only even-strand states: four classical and eight virtual word-pattern schemes, with strand tags and syntactic support restrictions.\n\nOrdinary oriented closure is retained. Both virtual exchange directions are included. Every unrestricted Markov edge lifts to a named even move under positive padding; no unspecified odd-intermediate path is a move-applicability condition. The complete proof verifies both closure preservation and completeness.\n\nThis is an elementary consequence of established classical and virtual Markov theorems. Historical novelty, minimality, and a stronger uniformly bounded-support locality property are unclaimed. It is not a plat, framed, or transverse theorem.\n\n## Independent review\nSeparate adversarial review: PASS for the full literal algebraic scope, with unchanged proof SHA-256 `749f55ab651476c5f3c7868fed2b9f06809a38518057e33414966cb6f4f253bc`.\n- 3,219 author assertions reproduced exactly\n- 6,641 independent assertions across 348 scheme instances\n- Both complete original-source versions and actual virtual exchange formulas checked\n\nThe proof, source audit, exact verifiers, receipts and unchanged review are included. These finite checks and independent AI review are not formal verification or human peer review. One substantive approach was used.\n","headRefName":"dot/math-10600042","headRefOid":"7260315f8b8b193020c09d4ef6df9d943a3a13ff","isDraft":true,"mergeable":"UNKNOWN","number":50,"state":"OPEN","title":"10600042: reviewed even-strand classical and virtual Markov reformulation","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/50"}
